.SH Files and authorization
On macOS, lab stores \f[CR]bootstrap.json\f[R], \f[CR]presets.enc\f[R]
and \f[CR]history.enc\f[R] under
\f[CR]\(ti/Library/Application Support/lab/\f[R].
On Linux the defaults are \f[CR]\(ti/.config/lab/bootstrap.json\f[R],
\f[CR]\(ti/.local/share/lab/presets.enc\f[R] and
\f[CR]\(ti/.local/state/lab/history.enc\f[R]; the corresponding XDG
directory variables apply.
Creation receipts are part of encrypted history.
Private profiles live in the absolute directory recorded by setup.
.PP
The bootstrap contains references and the profiles directory.
Credentials remain in 1Password; the Service Account Token is held by
the authorized process and is not saved.
Each session has an absolute lifetime, including time spent asleep,
configured by \f[CR]session.max_age_seconds\f[R] in the index.
There is no idle timeout.
.PP
Shell and editor clients receive a temporary credential capability tied
to the live lab process.
They are trusted local clients.
Disconnecting blocks lab\(cqs routes and grants; it cannot revoke a
cluster token that another client has already copied.
The local user account, installed code, terminal and editor extensions
must be trusted.
.SH Troubleshooting
\f[B]No clusters are registered:\f[R] prepare a private profile and run
\f[CR]lab cluster add\f[R].
Repeating \f[CR]lab init\f[R] is unnecessary when the index is already
configured.
.PP
\f[B]Profile missing or invalid:\f[R] check the configured directory,
the exact cluster ID and the \f[CR].yaml\f[R] extension.
Creation and creation retry need a valid profile; listing and accessing
existing Notebooks do not.
.PP
\f[B]1Password read\-back differs:\f[R] save the complete proposed
document in the correct item, then use Recheck.
Inspect the saved index before retrying a cancelled verification.
.PP
\f[B]Copy is unavailable:\f[R] install \f[CR]wl\-copy\f[R],
\f[CR]xclip\f[R] or \f[CR]xsel\f[R] on Linux.
macOS uses its built\-in \f[CR]pbcopy\f[R].
You can also select and copy the document manually.
.PP
\f[B]Notebook is not Ready:\f[R] inspect status and the reported Pod
state.
A readiness timeout does not delete or stop the Notebook.
If creation\(cqs outcome is uncertain, use its operation ID to reconcile
before creating anything else.
.PP
\f[B]Editor disconnected:\f[R] keep the owning lab process running.
Use Reconnect after a connection loss while authorization is still
valid.
After exiting lab or expiry, authorize a new session and open a new
editor window.
.PP
\f[B]Local encrypted data cannot be read:\f[R] preserve the files and
check the selected encryption key and file permissions.
lab does not reset corrupt or wrong\-key data.
.PP
\f[B]Manual not found:\f[R] follow the manual installation instructions
in the checkout\(cqs README, then check \f[CR]man \-w lab\f[R].
.SH See also
\f[CR]lab \-\-help\f[R], \f[CR]lab notebook COMMAND \-\-help\f[R],
\f[CR]kubectl(1)\f[R], \f[CR]ssh(1)\f[R].
.PP
The source checkout includes \f[CR]docs/configuration.md\f[R] for
configuration formats and \f[CR]docs/architecture.md\f[R] for the
implementation and development workflow.
